WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.296 --> 00:00:02.455
My name's Caitlin Brodnick and I'm here

00:00:02.455 --> 00:00:04.485
and healthy which is
like a really big deal.

00:00:04.485 --> 00:00:08.352
I tested positive for the
BRCA1 genetic mutation

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:10.753
which means that I have a very high risk

00:00:10.753 --> 00:00:14.336
of developing breast
cancer in my lifetime.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.092
I got tested at 25 because he's the

00:00:25.092 --> 00:00:27.082
only surviving person in his family.

00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:29.784
They've all died of cancers,
both parents and both sisters.

00:00:29.784 --> 00:00:31.756
I was about to lose my
insurance so I was like,

00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:34.367
okay fine I'll go get
tested and I went in to see

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.156
if I had a gluten allergy
and they were like no.

00:00:37.156 --> 00:00:39.395
You should really get
tested to see if you have

00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:42.125
like this breast cancer
gene as they call it

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.625
and so I was, I tested positive for BRCA1.

00:00:47.004 --> 00:00:49.590
When you are high risk, when you're BRCA,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.061
your medical folder gets red tagged

00:00:52.061 --> 00:00:54.540
and you kind of go to
the head of the class.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.331
So that meant that not
only did I have a mammogram

00:00:57.331 --> 00:00:59.304
when I was younger than the average woman,

00:00:59.304 --> 00:01:03.314
but I had this MRI where
they put a contrast dye

00:01:03.314 --> 00:01:05.955
in you and then once
the dye's in your body

00:01:05.955 --> 00:01:08.410
you do an MRI and then they can check

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.853
and see if anything's off.

00:01:09.853 --> 00:01:11.608
Then you have to wait for
like other information

00:01:11.608 --> 00:01:13.196
and that whole process of like sitting

00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:15.540
in a hospital, waiting for an MRI,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.913
having all of it just
really freaked me out

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.057
and I just didn't want
to be in that center.

00:01:22.057 --> 00:01:23.457
I didn't want to be
next to cancer patients

00:01:23.457 --> 00:01:24.714
cause I felt horrible.

00:01:24.714 --> 00:01:27.080
I felt guilty that I was
taking time away from them.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.247
So I just ran away from it completely.

00:01:31.437 --> 00:01:32.726
The whole thing I was like, okay

00:01:32.726 --> 00:01:34.606
I'm not getting surveillance,
I hate my breasts

00:01:34.606 --> 00:01:37.477
and they're really affecting my body and

00:01:37.477 --> 00:01:39.704
my self esteem and I'm pretty miserable

00:01:39.704 --> 00:01:41.447
and at the time doctors
were just suggesting

00:01:41.447 --> 00:01:43.246
that women if they choose to have

00:01:43.246 --> 00:01:45.129
a mastectomy preventatively, it's after

00:01:45.129 --> 00:01:47.198
they're finished breast feeding,

00:01:47.198 --> 00:01:49.305
once they're into menopause.

00:01:49.305 --> 00:01:52.306
So I told my family and
they were all really shocked

00:01:52.306 --> 00:01:54.187
but as I explained it and explained

00:01:54.187 --> 00:01:57.011
how I didn't feel authentic in my body,

00:01:57.011 --> 00:02:00.058
I felt like I was hiding, I
was not going to the doctor,

00:02:00.058 --> 00:02:02.885
it made a lot more sense to everyone.

00:02:02.885 --> 00:02:05.123
To have the surgery,
basically what they do

00:02:05.123 --> 00:02:07.043
is they remove all of the breast tissue

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:09.149
because all of those
cells have a high risk

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:12.727
of becoming cancerous
and for that they remove

00:02:12.727 --> 00:02:14.465
all of the breast tissue but

00:02:14.465 --> 00:02:16.109
they don't go into the chest wall.

00:02:16.109 --> 00:02:17.626
Your pec muscle stays intact.

00:02:17.626 --> 00:02:19.304
You can choose to
rebuild or not to rebuild

00:02:19.304 --> 00:02:21.713
and I did not know what
to choose so for me

00:02:21.713 --> 00:02:23.330
I wanted to go really gradually because

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.747
I could not choose, like I had no concept.

00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:28.466
I know I wanted small
breasts, smaller breasts

00:02:28.466 --> 00:02:30.703
but like I was sick of looking
like a Russian nesting doll.

00:02:30.703 --> 00:02:32.452
I wanted to look like a Russian ballerina.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:35.534
Like I just wanted to
feel light and easy and

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.467
fun but I also had no
idea what I was doing

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.884
and I actually had to
convince a couple doctors

00:02:40.884 --> 00:02:42.927
that this was the right decision for me,

00:02:42.927 --> 00:02:46.694
that it was giving me a lot of
anxiety with my now husband.

00:02:46.694 --> 00:02:49.910
Doctors told me that I
had a less than 1% chance

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.055
after I had my surgery
and I think it can change

00:02:52.055 --> 00:02:53.755
based on women keep their nipples or

00:02:53.755 --> 00:02:55.703
not keep their nipples, but they told me

00:02:55.703 --> 00:02:58.244
less than 1% which is great but I still

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.117
have a risk of ovarian cancer and

00:03:01.117 --> 00:03:03.774
with this mutation I have an elevated risk

00:03:03.774 --> 00:03:06.607
of pancreatic cancer and melanoma.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:14.431
That was something that
was a little difficult

00:03:14.431 --> 00:03:16.296
to handle in the beginning because

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.871
when you think of having a preventative

00:03:17.871 --> 00:03:20.046
double mastectomy you hear that and

00:03:20.046 --> 00:03:22.060
it feels like it's a one time deal.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.922
Just like you'd have knee surgery or

00:03:23.922 --> 00:03:26.443
you'd have a replacement, the thing with

00:03:26.443 --> 00:03:29.349
this type of surgery is because they are

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:31.324
removing body parts
and adding new implants

00:03:31.324 --> 00:03:33.022
and your body's changing, it takes

00:03:33.022 --> 00:03:34.647
a lot longer than you'd realize.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.777
So going through the second surgery was

00:03:36.777 --> 00:03:39.105
really confusing to me in a way because

00:03:39.105 --> 00:03:41.097
I had no idea what it would be like

00:03:41.097 --> 00:03:43.603
but I still had this really recent memory

00:03:43.603 --> 00:03:46.167
of how it felt right as soon as I woke up

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:49.063
from surgery or how it hurt
to move my arm at first

00:03:49.063 --> 00:03:51.154
and so my doctor said it was really common

00:03:51.154 --> 00:03:54.126
that you would have these
fears that were sort of

00:03:54.126 --> 00:03:57.456
these fresh feeling fears
but at the same time

00:03:57.456 --> 00:03:59.828
you don't actually know how you'll feel.

00:03:59.828 --> 00:04:03.710
So it's this like bizarre,
premature nervousness

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.537
and so that surgery happened and it was

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:07.257
a lot easier than my first surgery because

00:04:07.257 --> 00:04:10.144
in the mastectomy surgery,
when they remove everything,

00:04:10.144 --> 00:04:12.715
your full chest just feels like it's been

00:04:12.715 --> 00:04:14.676
ripped apart but just like

00:04:14.676 --> 00:04:16.978
it sounds disgusting, but you're fine.

00:04:16.978 --> 00:04:19.124
It's bandaged, you're on meds, it's okay.

00:04:19.124 --> 00:04:21.012
But your chest, your body really

00:04:21.012 --> 00:04:22.313
feels like it was assaulted.

00:04:22.313 --> 00:04:24.113
Like it really has to heal and in

00:04:24.113 --> 00:04:26.180
the second surgery its a little less so.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.728
You know, there's less
movement of the muscles.

00:04:28.728 --> 00:04:30.736
There's less things that have to rebuild,

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.531
also when you have surgery like this when

00:04:34.531 --> 00:04:36.322
they remove the tissue they also severe

00:04:36.322 --> 00:04:37.966
a bunch of nerves so you really don't

00:04:37.966 --> 00:04:39.597
have any feeling in your breasts.

00:04:39.597 --> 00:04:41.868
So that was kind of a
crazy thing to no longer

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.524
have any feeling and
doctors told me that like

00:04:44.524 --> 00:04:46.877
I couldn't wear, put like a hot compress

00:04:46.877 --> 00:04:49.301
for too long or they
said you can't cook over

00:04:49.301 --> 00:04:51.451
an open flame because
you might not feel it.

00:04:51.451 --> 00:04:53.374
Also you can't wear underwire bras because

00:04:53.374 --> 00:04:56.248
the bra might poke you
and you might not feel it.

00:04:56.248 --> 00:04:59.339
Now years later I can feel pretty well

00:04:59.339 --> 00:05:01.026
and my nerves have grown back but

00:05:01.026 --> 00:05:03.712
in the beginning they
were very, very cautious.

00:05:03.712 --> 00:05:05.405
If a friend asks me, should I get tested?

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:06.715
Do I need to get tested?

00:05:06.715 --> 00:05:08.668
I always say, you can talk to your doctor.

00:05:08.668 --> 00:05:09.848
They'll advise you.

00:05:09.848 --> 00:05:11.410
You know it's up to you to get tested,

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.770
but that's a lot of information and

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.095
even though you might not have cancer

00:05:15.095 --> 00:05:17.245
that diagnosis feels, sometimes

00:05:17.245 --> 00:05:19.134
you feel like you have cancer.

00:05:19.134 --> 00:05:22.243
It's around the corner and
its really hard to shake that

00:05:22.243 --> 00:05:26.094
and so once you know, I
think it's helpful to know

00:05:26.094 --> 00:05:27.685
and you can empower yourself but also

00:05:27.685 --> 00:05:29.794
it's good to know, like,
is this information

00:05:29.794 --> 00:05:33.193
going to just destroy me right
now because it did for me.

00:05:33.193 --> 00:05:35.579
It was just too much and
it's such a crazy feeling

00:05:35.579 --> 00:05:37.344
to have the second surgery and now to

00:05:37.344 --> 00:05:40.717
love my body more which sounds insane,

00:05:40.717 --> 00:05:43.536
like it sounds crazy and
if somebody said that

00:05:43.536 --> 00:05:45.233
to me I don't know if I'd believe them

00:05:45.233 --> 00:05:46.888
and I don't know if they
were just on some pink cloud

00:05:46.888 --> 00:05:49.752
and just decided they
were lying to themselves

00:05:49.752 --> 00:05:53.016
but I really feel so
much better in my body

00:05:53.016 --> 00:05:55.734
and so much calmer and I never think of

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:58.352
breast cancer and I'm just really happy

00:05:58.352 --> 00:06:00.664
that my kids aren't going to have to see

00:06:00.664 --> 00:06:04.383
their mom go through breast cancer.

00:06:04.383 --> 00:06:07.466
(instrumental music)

